<Project>

  <!-- The version numbers, kept in a file of their own so that raising them is not itself a change
       to Core: .github/scripts/check-versions.ps1 compares Core against its last release and
       leaves this file out.

       Releases are numbered from one sequence. Controls takes every number. Core takes a number
       only in a release that changes it, and then the same one as Controls, so Core may skip some:

         1.0.0  Controls 1.0.0  Core 1.0.0   first release
         1.0.1  Controls 1.0.1  Core 1.0.1   Core changed, so both
         1.0.2  Controls 1.0.2  Core 1.0.1   Controls alone
         1.0.3  Controls 1.0.3  Core 1.0.3   Core changed: the next free number, not 1.0.2

       "Core" here is SumireCraft.Maui.Core. SumireCraft.Core, the package that depends on no UI
       framework, is numbered the same way and on its own: it takes a number only in a release
       that changes it, whether or not Core changes too. It was first released in 1.1.0.

       So SumireVersion is the release, and the tag is v$(SumireVersion). SumireCoreVersion and
       SumireCraftCoreVersion are each either the same or the version of an earlier release, whose
       tag the same script diffs against.
       Controls names each Core it was built with as its minimum, because packing reads their own
       Version through the project references, and the next major version of Controls as the
       bound (BoundCoreDependency in the Controls project). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <SumireVersion>1.1.0</SumireVersion>
    <SumireCoreVersion>1.1.0</SumireCoreVersion>
    <SumireCraftCoreVersion>1.1.0</SumireCraftCoreVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
